{"schemaVersion":1,"skill":{"id":"k-dense-ai--scientific-agent-skills--relsa-severity-assessment","name":"relsa-severity-assessment","description":"Supports multivariate severity assessment and exploratory endpoint-time score forecasting for laboratory animal studies using the RELSA (RELative Severity Assessment) score and ARIMA-based foRcast forecasting. Use when combining welfare readouts — body weight or weight loss, body temperature, clinical or nesting scores, biomarkers, activity, heart rate, burrowing, wheel running — into one severity score per animal per day, when asking which animals are at risk of reaching a humane endpoint at a specified future observation time, when defining attention/danger zones or thresholds on a severity scale by kernel density estimation, or when reporting severity for a 3Rs, refinement, animal-welfare, or EU Directive 2010/63/EU severity-assessment context. Covers directionality (\"turned\" variables), baseline normalization, reference sets, RELSA weights, ARIMA prediction intervals, and RMSE/PICP/MPIW evaluation.","category":"Development","tags":["relsa","severity","assessment","supports","multivariate","exploratory","endpoint","time","score","forecasting","laboratory","animal","studies","relative","arima","based","forcast","forecasting."],"repo":"K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills","owner":"K-Dense-AI","stars":48508,"official":false,"featured":false,"license":"MIT","licensePath":"LICENSE.md","revision":"a1043ef544e3a100c28e70a736b6cf32554d0677","path":"skills/relsa-severity-assessment","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills/tree/a1043ef544e3a100c28e70a736b6cf32554d0677/skills/relsa-severity-assessment","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T11:14:06.196Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-12T09:43:29Z","fileCount":10,"bytes":127395,"sha256":"10ee1a904565f5e9c9d432b3af136db42927d0811f07f646355600fec6633f8a","historical":false},"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","sourcePath":"skills/relsa-severity-assessment/SKILL.md","bytes":20981,"sha2